{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"test-runner","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Test Runner","description":"Run all tests, this file, or the test under the cursor, and run the last one again. Detects Vitest, Jest, Mocha, pytest, cargo, go, PHPUnit, Pest, Maven, Gradle and RSpec.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:testRunner.all","onCommand:testRunner.file","onCommand:testRunner.nearest","onCommand:testRunner.rerun","onCommand:testRunner.watch","onCommand:testRunner.coverage","onCommand:testRunner.detect"],"permissions":["terminal","workspace.read"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"testRunner.all","title":"Run All Tests","category":"Test Runner"},{"command":"testRunner.file","title":"Run Tests in This File","category":"Test Runner"},{"command":"testRunner.nearest","title":"Run the Test Under Cursor","category":"Test Runner"},{"command":"testRunner.rerun","title":"Run the Last Test Command Again","category":"Test Runner"},{"command":"testRunner.watch","title":"Watch Tests in This File","category":"Test Runner"},{"command":"testRunner.coverage","title":"Run All Tests with Coverage","category":"Test Runner"},{"command":"testRunner.detect","title":"Which Test Tool Does This Project Use?","category":"Test Runner"}],"keybindings":[{"command":"testRunner.nearest","key":"Ctrl+Alt+Shift+T"},{"command":"testRunner.rerun","key":"Ctrl+Alt+Shift+R"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Test Runner: run all tests, the tests of this file, or the test under the cursor, then run the last one again.\n// It looks at your project to choose the tool (Vitest, Jest, Mocha, pytest, cargo test, go test, PHPUnit and Pest, Maven, Gradle, RSpec)\n// and types the command in the terminal, where you see the result.\n\n/** Which test tool a project uses, from the contents of its marker files. Returns { tool, label } or null. */\nfunction detect(files) {\n  const has = (n) => Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(files, n) && files[n] !== null;\n  if (has('package.json')) {\n    let pkg = {};\n    try { pkg = JSON.parse(files['package.json']); } catch { pkg = {}; }\n    const deps = { ...(pkg.dependencies || {}), ...(pkg.devDependencies || {}) };\n    if (deps.vitest) return { tool: 'vitest', label: 'Vitest' };\n    if (deps.jest || deps['ts-jest']) return { tool: 'jest', label: 'Jest' };\n    if (deps.mocha) return { tool: 'mocha', label: 'Mocha' };\n    if (pkg.scripts && /node\\s+--test/.test(pkg.scripts.test || '')) return { tool: 'nodetest', label: 'Node test runner' };\n    if (pkg.scripts && pkg.scripts.test) return { tool: 'npm', label: 'npm test' };\n  }\n  if (has('Cargo.toml')) return { tool: 'cargo', label: 'cargo test' };\n  if (has('go.mod')) return { tool: 'go', label: 'go test' };\n  if (has('composer.json')) {\n    let c = {};\n    try { c = JSON.parse(files['composer.json']); } catch { c = {}; }\n    const deps = { ...(c.require || {}), ...(c['require-dev'] || {}) };\n    if (deps['pestphp/pest']) return { tool: 'pest', label: 'Pest' };\n    if (deps['phpunit/phpunit']) return { tool: 'phpunit', label: 'PHPUnit' };\n  }\n  if (has('pytest.ini') || has('pyproject.toml') || has('setup.cfg') || has('requirements.txt') || has('tox.ini')) return { tool: 'pytest', label: 'pytest' };\n  if (has('pom.xml')) return { tool: 'maven', label: 'Maven' };\n  if (has('build.gradle') || has('build.gradle.kts')) return { tool: 'gradle', label: 'Gradle' };\n  if (has('Gemfile')) return { tool: 'rspec', label: 'RSpec' };\n  return null;\n}\n\nconst MARKERS = ['package.json', 'Cargo.toml', 'go.mod', 'composer.json', 'pytest.ini', 'pyproject.toml', 'setup.cfg', 'requirements.txt', 'tox.ini', 'pom.xml', 'build.gradle', 'build.gradle.kts', 'Gemfile'];\n\n/** The name of the test that holds line `line` (0 based), looking upward. Returns { name, kind } or null. */\nfunction nearestTest(text, line, family) {\n  const lines = text.split('\\n');\n  for (let i = Math.min(line, lines.length - 1); i >= 0; i--) {\n    const l = lines[i];\n    let m;\n    if (family === 'js' && (m = /\\b(?:it|test)(?:\\.(?:only|skip|each\\([^)]*\\)))?\\(\\s*(['\"`])(.+?)\\1/.exec(l))) return { name: m[2], kind: 'test' };\n    if (family === 'js' && (m = /\\bdescribe(?:\\.(?:only|skip))?\\(\\s*(['\"`])(.+?)\\1/.exec(l))) return { name: m[2], kind: 'suite' };\n    if (family === 'py' && (m = /^\\s*(?:async\\s+)?def\\s+(test\\w*)\\s*\\(/.exec(l))) return { name: m[1], kind: 'test' };\n    if (family === 'py' && (m = /^class\\s+(Test\\w*)/.exec(l))) return { name: m[1], kind: 'suite' };\n    if (family === 'go' && (m = /^func\\s+(Test\\w*)\\s*\\(/.exec(l))) return { name: m[1], kind: 'test' };\n    if (family === 'rust' && (m = /^\\s*(?:async\\s+)?fn\\s+(\\w+)\\s*\\(/.exec(l)) && i > 0 && lines.slice(Math.max(0, i - 3), i).some((x) => /#\\[(?:tokio::)?test/.test(x))) return { name: m[1], kind: 'test' };\n    if (family === 'php' && (m = /\\bfunction\\s+(test\\w+)\\s*\\(/.exec(l))) return { name: m[1], kind: 'test' };\n    if (family === 'php' && (m = /\\b(?:it|test)\\(\\s*(['\"])(.+?)\\1/.exec(l))) return { name: m[2], kind: 'test' };\n    if (family === 'java' && (m = /\\bvoid\\s+(\\w+)\\s*\\(/.exec(l)) && lines.slice(Math.max(0, i - 3), i + 1).some((x) => /@Test/.test(x))) return { name: m[1], kind: 'test' };\n    if (family === 'ruby' && (m = /^\\s*(?:it|example|scenario)\\s+['\"](.+?)['\"]/.exec(l))) return { name: m[1], kind: 'test' };\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nconst familyOf = (path) => ({ js: 'js', jsx: 'js', ts: 'js', tsx: 'js', mjs: 'js', cjs: 'js', py: 'py', go: 'go', rs: 'rust', php: 'php', java: 'java', kt: 'java', rb: 'ruby' })[String(path).split('.').pop().toLowerCase()] || null;\n\nconst bad = (s) => /[\"\\n\\r$`]/.test(String(s));\nconst q = (s) => '\"' + s + '\"';\nconst dirOf = (rel) => (rel.includes('/') ? rel.slice(0, rel.lastIndexOf('/')) : '.');\n\n/**\n * Builds the command. `scope` is all, file or test. `rel` is the file path from the project folder with / separators.\n * Returns null when it cannot be done (for example a test name cannot be put in a command safely).\n */\nfunction command(tool, scope, rel, test, opts = {}) {\n  const w = opts.watch;\n  const cov = opts.coverage;\n  if (rel && bad(rel)) return null;\n  if (test && bad(test.name)) return null;\n  const name = test ? test.name : null;\n  switch (tool) {\n    case 'vitest': return ['npx vitest', w ? '' : 'run', cov ? '--coverage' : '', scope !== 'all' ? q(rel) : '', scope === 'test' ? '-t ' + q(name) : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    case 'jest': return ['npx jest', w ? '--watch' : '', cov ? '--coverage' : '', scope !== 'all' ? q(rel) : '', scope === 'test' ? '-t ' + q(name) : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    case 'mocha': return ['npx mocha', w ? '--watch' : '', scope !== 'all' ? q(rel) : '', scope === 'test' ? '-g ' + q(name) : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    case 'nodetest': return ['node --test', w ? '--watch' : '', scope !== 'all' ? q(rel) : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    case 'npm': return scope === 'all' ? 'npm test' : 'npm test -- ' + q(rel);\n    case 'cargo': return ['cargo test', scope === 'test' ? name : '', scope === 'file' ? q(rel.replace(/^.*\\/(?=[^/]+$)/, '').replace(/\\.rs$/, '')) : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    case 'go': return scope === 'all' ? 'go test ./...' : scope === 'file' ? 'go test ' + q('./' + dirOf(rel)) : 'go test ' + q('./' + dirOf(rel)) + ' -run ' + q('^' + name + '$');\n    case 'pytest': return ['python -m pytest', cov ? '--cov' : '', scope !== 'all' ? q(rel + (scope === 'test' ? '::' + name : '')) : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    case 'pest': return ['./vendor/bin/pest', scope !== 'all' ? q(rel) : '', scope === 'test' ? '--filter ' + q(name) : '', cov ? '--coverage' : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    case 'phpunit': return ['./vendor/bin/phpunit', scope !== 'all' ? q(rel) : '', scope === 'test' ? '--filter ' + q(name) : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    case 'maven': {\n      if (scope === 'all') return 'mvn test';\n      const cls = rel.split('/').pop().replace(/\\.\\w+$/, '');\n      return 'mvn test -Dtest=' + (scope === 'test' ? cls + '#' + name : cls);\n    }\n    case 'gradle': {\n      if (scope === 'all') return './gradlew test';\n      const cls = rel.split('/').pop().replace(/\\.\\w+$/, '');\n      return './gradlew test --tests ' + q(scope === 'test' ? '*' + cls + '.' + name : '*' + cls);\n    }\n    case 'rspec': return ['bundle exec rspec', scope !== 'all' ? q(rel) : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' ');\n    default: return null;\n  }\n}\n\nexports._test = { detect, nearestTest, command, familyOf, MARKERS };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  const reg = (id, fn) => context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register(id, fn));\n  const key = () => 'last:' + (ferrum.workspace.root || '');\n\n  async function project() {\n    if (!ferrum.workspace.root) { ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a folder first.', 'warn'); return null; }\n    const files = {};\n    for (const m of MARKERS) {\n      try { files[m] = await ferrum.workspace.readFile(m); } catch { files[m] = null; }\n    }\n    const found = detect(files);\n    if (!found) ferrum.window.showMessage('I could not tell which test tool this project uses. Looked for package.json, Cargo.toml, go.mod, composer.json, pyproject.toml, pom.xml, build.gradle and Gemfile.', 'warn');\n    return found;\n  }\n\n  const relPath = (p) => {\n    const root = (ferrum.workspace.root || '').replace(/\\\\/g, '/').replace(/\\/$/, '');\n    const f = String(p || '').replace(/\\\\/g, '/');\n    return root && f.startsWith(root + '/') ? f.slice(root.length + 1) : f;\n  };\n\n  async function run(scope, opts = {}) {\n    const found = await project();\n    if (!found) return;\n    let rel = '';\n    let test = null;\n    if (scope !== 'all') {\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\n      if (!doc || !doc.path) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open and save a test file first.', 'warn');\n      rel = relPath(doc.path);\n      if (scope === 'test') {\n        const fam = familyOf(doc.path);\n        test = fam ? nearestTest(doc.text, doc.selection.start.line, fam) : null;\n        if (!test) return ferrum.window.showMessage('I could not find a test around the cursor. Put the cursor inside a test.', 'warn');\n        if (test.kind === 'suite' && found.tool !== 'vitest' && found.tool !== 'jest' && found.tool !== 'mocha' && found.tool !== 'pytest') scope = 'file';\n      }\n      if (doc.dirty) await ferrum.commands.execute('file.save');\n    }\n    const cmd = command(found.tool, scope, rel, test, opts);\n    if (!cmd) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Cannot build a safe command for that name or file.', 'warn');\n    await ferrum.storage.set(key(), cmd);\n    ferrum.window.showMessage(found.label + ': ' + (scope === 'all' ? 'all tests' : scope === 'file' ? rel : test.name));\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\n  }\n\n  reg('testRunner.all', () => run('all'));\n  reg('testRunner.file', () => run('file'));\n  reg('testRunner.nearest', () => run('test'));\n  reg('testRunner.watch', () => run('file', { watch: true }));\n  reg('testRunner.coverage', () => run('all', { coverage: true }));\n  reg('testRunner.rerun', async () => {\n    const cmd = await ferrum.storage.get(key(), null);\n    if (!cmd) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Nothing to run again yet. Run a test first.');\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\n  });\n  reg('testRunner.detect', async () => {\n    const found = await project();\n    if (found) ferrum.window.showMessage('This project uses ' + found.label + '.');\n  });\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Test Runner\n\nThree shortcuts that save you typing test commands: **Run All Tests**, **Run Tests in This File** and **Run the Test Under Cursor**, plus **Run the Last Test Command Again** and, where the tool supports it, **Watch** and **Coverage**.\n\nIt looks at your project to choose the tool: `package.json` (Vitest, Jest, Mocha, `node --test` or the `test` script), `Cargo.toml` (cargo test), `go.mod` (go test), `composer.json` (Pest or PHPUnit), Python files (pytest), `pom.xml` (Maven), `build.gradle` (Gradle) and `Gemfile` (RSpec).\n\nThe test under the cursor is found by looking upward from the cursor for `it(` / `test(` / `describe(`, `def test_`, `#[test] fn`, `func TestX`, `function testX`, `@Test` or RSpec `it`. If no test is found it tells you instead of running everything.\n\nThe command is **typed in the terminal** where you see the result, and unsaved changes are saved first. Do not run it while a program that reads keys is active in that terminal.\n\n## Permissions\n\n**terminal**, and **workspace.read** to read the marker files (`package.json` and the like).\n"}}}